Project: Our project will use data from the FDA’s openFDA Drug Adverse Event API (collected in Python via requests, 999 reports) to study 
adverse drug events (ADE's). ADE's cause over 1.5 million emergency-department visits a year in the U.S., and a large majority affect 
older adults who take more medications. We will examine how patient and medication characteristics (age, sex, number of drugs, and 
number of reported reactions) relate to whether a report is classified as serious versus non-serious. We also plan to build a 
classification model to predict whether a report is serious, with the goal of identifying patterns that could help with 
drug-safety monitoring.

